WEBVTT

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.390
No matter how much time passes the summer heat never changes.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.000
That's why this season reminds me...

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.640
...of when I was thirteen. 
 Naive and carefree.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.140
That still doesn't change to this day.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:05.290
- You've grown up quite a bit Hajime-chan!  
 - It's already been five years, huh?

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:10.500
- You're going to keep on growing. Surpassing me.  
- Arashi-san?!

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.030
Hajime-chan. I have to say goodbye.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:19.010
- What are you saying Arashi-san! 
- We can't continue this. It's too unnatural.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.010
I have to, when the cut is shallow.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:25.970
No! 
 As long as I live...

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.930
...I decided to stay with you, Arashi-san!

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.510
- That's not true.  
- No, I'm serious!

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:35.540
It's about next summer.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:40.710
Next summer you're not going to visit me.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.150
No way!
 That can't be true!

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.800
It's true. 
 I came to this time period connected to another boy.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.030
It's something that's already decided in the future.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:55.950
To me it's history but...

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:01.130
-...to you, it's destiny.  
- This can't be.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.760
- I came here to follow through on my promise. 
- Promise?!

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.390
You told me you'll give it back to me.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.710
You promised, right?

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:22.120
What was I supposed to give back to her? 
 Was it this?

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:27.570
Give back--- give back--- 
Man I can't remember!

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.410
It's like this.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:32.720
That's right! 
 I'm so slow.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:34.930
How could I forget a character like this.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:42.760
- You have to tell me you're in here Arashi-san!  
- Good morning Hajime-chan!

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:47.320
You Guys are Kiwi, Papaya, and Mango

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.960
What's wrong Kaya?

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.300
It's nothing.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.010
Hajime-chan did you pull a prank on her again?

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.010
I didn't do anything!

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:09.530
- How regretful!  
- See! You did something!

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.780
I didn't do anything! Please believe me!

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:16.970
- Anyway. Kaya, where's the milk?  
- I don't know!

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:19.020
Hey, you know.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:24.010
You time traveled to get the milk before it was spoiled.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.310
Where is it?

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.160
I told you I don't know!

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.770
Master, did you tell her to do something outrageous again?

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:35.230
It's not outrageous.
 I was thinking about the environment.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:45.240
It's hard to confess that she made herself drink the spoiled drink.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.010
Is it not possible to change history that is already set?

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.670
Kaya was able to take the expired milk to the past but...

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.920
...she couldn't change the circumstance.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.430
- That's reality. 
 - So you can't change destiny, huh?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.010
Yes, simply said.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:07.480
- How boring. 
 - Destiny, huh?

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:11.700
Why are you all serious?

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:15.280
Shut up! 
 There's times that I contemplate my thoughts too!

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.280
Hey, let me go!

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.020
Man, it's really hot out there.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:33.320
- Thanks so much. 
 - Can't believe how you treat me sometimes.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.250
Don't make your customers go run errands.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:39.110
No big deal. It was on your way here.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:43.700
- Wow, kiwis! 
 - Looks delicious!

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.350
I had him buy it because it was on sale.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:55.670
<i>The day has come! 
 I can unravel my new creation that I made amid past failures!</i>

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.650
<i>It's the time to debut it!</i>

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.020
This might look like a normal kiwi but...

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:05.920
...it's a super spicy "kiwi bomb!"

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.090
Going by scoville units...

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:11.990
Tabasco is 2,500 scoville.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:16.540
Red peppers are 50,000 scovilles.
Habanero and hot mustard are 300,000 scovilles.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:20.710
But this one is 2,000,000 scovilles!

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:25.630
It's equivalent to Tobasco sauce for 100 pizzas!

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:30.330
This is the ultimate weapon! 
 "Cutie Q-chan!"

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:34.180
Yamashiro, the guy that tries to get close with Arashi-san.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.900
I must serve punishment to him as a man!

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:41.000
This time I will make Yamashiro eat this!

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.510
- May I have sa--  
- Here you go.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.290
Salt!

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.430
Are you really going to do this?

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:54.910
Of course Jun. 
This is to punish him for humiliating me twice!

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:59.470
- I will redeem myself this time. 
- The second time was your fault.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.390
Hajime was at fault for that!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:07.310
I will let him know that revenge over food is chilling!

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:14.270
I've gathered the spiciest ingredients from around the world to make this sauce!

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:19.290
I will now put this into the kiwi.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:24.910
I'm finished when I put the lid on and close it with tape.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:29.750
- Tape? 
- He won't notice because it's clear.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.100
Wow! The technique has overcome technology!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.450
Hajime, face your doom!

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:40.600
When you taste this, you'll taste revenge!

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:46.590
It seems very hot.
 How many scovilles is it?

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.820
I don't know.
 But it's very scoville hot.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.210
What could this be?

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:00.120
A diagram for "Cutie Q-chan?"

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.990
What's Hajime-chan going to do with this?

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:08.330
I have an idea! 
 I'll make one and surprise Hajime-chan!

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:11.260
I can make a good one!

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:16.420
<i>The store is filled with kiwis today.</i>

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:19.210
<i>They've bought quite a few.</i>

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:23.260
<i>Even if you make rice seasoning, it won't be gone.</i>

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:27.540
<i>Better not make me eat it everyday! 
 If you eat too much...</i>

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.320
<i>You might be hairy like a kiwi.</i>

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:35.830
I want this one. 
 "Kiwi Sundae"

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.180
I got it.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:42.430
- I have an order Kanako! 
- Let's get started on it, Yayoi.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:44.890
What's the name of this dish?!

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:49.380
It's--- I forget the name of the dish.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.640
Can you let me know what kind of dish it is?

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:54.920
Yes. 
For sure!

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:58.760
It's a dish filled with refreshing colors.

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:02.140
A fruit that is round like the sun and green.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.530
With a juiciness and a slight tanginess.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:09.000
Combined with a cool cream, it plays out a scene in the summer.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:13.930
As in the name, it replicates the joy of "Sunday."

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.630
It's a cup filled with joy.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:20.500
- What a joy filled dish!
- What?!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:23.850
- Do you know of such a dish?!  
- Hey!

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.790
- Of course. I know.
- Hey, wait!

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.470
- Let's go and make it.  
- Hey how did you come to that conclusion?!

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.880
I told you I wanted a "Kiwi Sundae!" 
 Hey!

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:38.380
Where's Yamashiro at?!

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.580
If it gets mixed up with the other kiwis it's going to be a problem!

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.120
I'm going to hide this in the back.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:54.530
Hajime you'll see what happens!

00:09:56.380 --> 00:10:01.090
Looks great! 
 I name it "Pretty Kiwi 7!"

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.550
I might have a talent for pulling off pranks!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.650
Oh my gosh! 
 There's Takakura Ken!

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:10.800
Takakura Ken?!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.230
- Ouch! 
 - Oh!

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:21.000
<i>Oh no! 
 I can't tell which one is mine!</i>

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:25.460
<i>If I get the wrong one, someone else is going to get my kiwi!</i>

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.840
<i>Oh no! What should I do?! 
 Oh well.</i>

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.920
- What?! 
 - They're making a move!

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:38.730
- What's wrong Hajime-chan? 
- Oh it's nothing!

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:44.270
They're connected.
 Good, I'll look for mine now.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:51.010
The tape is coming off the kiwi! 
 It's that one!

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.710
Welcome.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:07.260
- Isn't that Takakura Ken?!  
- Hey! Go get an autograph sheet!

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:11.000
- What?!
- We're going to get his autograph and put it on the wall here.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:16.230
- I just ordered a drink right now!  
- I'll comp it for you, so go.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.500
Oh, what are these doing here?

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:26.850
Natsu No Arashi

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:35.750
- Man, that caught me off guard. 
 It's because you grabbed my hand suddenly.

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:39.400
- I didn't know what happened.  
- I'm sorry.

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:42.190
It's not there!

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.110
Takakura Ken to Hakobune.

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:48.560
Thank you for waiting. 
 It's a dish filled with refreshing colors.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:51.830
A fruit that is round like the sun and green.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:56.750
A perfect combination of juiciness and sweet tanginess matching the creaminess.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.000
It plays a scene out from the summertime.

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:03.110
As in the name, it replicates the joy of "Sunday."

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:08.780
- It's a glass full of joy!  
- Could this be a kiwi sundae?!

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:13.390
- Is this what you ordered?! 
- This can't be! This is exactly what I ordered!

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:18.310
- What are you saying? Of course it is.  
- I'm surprised because it's abnormal!

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.400
What a weirdo. 
 Are you going to eat it or not?!

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.150
I'll eat it. 
 I ordered it.

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:34.620
- What are you doing?  
- <i>Oh no, there's the kiwi that I made.</i>

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:38.120
<i>My "Cutie Q-Chan" hit Sunglasses, huh?</i>

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:40.660
<i>I'm sorry Hideo-san.</i>

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:44.650
But it's a blessing in disguise that it didn't hit anyone else.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:50.080
I'm glad it hit Sunglasses. 
 What?! How do you know?!

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:52.600
I feel something bad is happening.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:58.470
What?! You guys made "Lovely Kiwi" too?!

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:03.000
No. Mine is called "Pretty Kiwi 7."

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.580
So where did the other two go?!

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.160
- Welcome.  
- Hey, how are you?!

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:15.310
It's really hot outside. 
 I feel like I'm going to get a heat stroke walking outside.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:17.540
Please, enjoy the cool air in here.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.790
<i>Dang it! Where were you!</i>

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.600
<i>It's all your fault because you were lagging!</i>

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:29.770
- What is this?  
- For you Yamashiro-san.

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:32.600
- It's a token of our appreciation.
- Oh...

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:36.650
...I should be the one thanking you for taking care of Josephine.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.330
This is a kiwi cream puff.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:42.770
I used a whole kiwi in it.

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:48.850
What a delightful cream puff. 
 When did you make it?

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:53.060
I just made it a few minutes ago. 
 There's more over there.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.630
Here try some!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:01.050
Oh, thanks. 
 I'll take one.

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:07.040
This isn't going to be good Kaya-san. 
 One of them might contain the "Lovely Kiwi."

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:14.970
- It's really delicious. 
- Thank you.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:18.000
I guess that wasn't the one.

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:21.000
How could fate be playing me like this.

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:25.510
What should I do?! 
Oh these wonderful kiwi cream puffs!

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:30.510
We're going to follow the same plan as before.

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:35.970
We'll switch out the "Cutie Kiwi" with a different one.

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:41.160
- Mine is "Lovely Kiwi."  
- Mine is "Pretty Kiwi 7."

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:45.840
If we switch it out before Yayoi-san makes it...

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:48.060
...we can avoid a disaster in this time period.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:52.990
That means I can eat that cream puff without worrying.

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:57.500
Wait. Murata-san already ate one. 
 What's going to happen to that one?!

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.420
If we switch it out wouldn't it contradict history?

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:03.550
No. History is already made.

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:07.540
Whatever we do, we won't be able to change it.

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:11.170
Inversely, if we look at it,
 we just need to switch the ones we can get to.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.770
I got it. Let's do it. 
 For the cream puffs!

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:30.860
- I finished making "Pretty Kiwi 7" right about now.  
- Look over there.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.980
Oh my gosh! 
 It's Takakura Ken!

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:37.840
Where?! 
Takakura Ken?!

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:46.040
Those three on the table. 
 Those are it!

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:50.700
I can see the tape coming off of Kaya-san's
 There's no doubt.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.200
Alright. I'll go get them.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:58.710
Hey Yayoi-san. 
 Look over there! There's Noguchi Goro!

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:01.770
Oh! There's Tonosama Kings over there!

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:06.400
I can't tell what Yayoi-san's into.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:10.160
Yayoi! Takakura Ken is really here!

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.930
- Really, Kanako?! 
 - Where's your handkerchief?!

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:17.830
I have it here! 
 I want him to wipe my sweat off.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:21.410
Perfect timing! 
 I'll get these now!

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:38.210
Alright. One is Kaya-san's and the other one is mine.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.870
We were only able to collect two.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.000
Don't we have to search for the other one?!

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.760
The one that's left is for Sunglasses to suffer from.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:51.000
- We can just let that one slide. 
- Yea, if his destiny is set already.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.870
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:57.010
Oh, good. 
That relieves me.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:07.640
Now we can eat this kiwi cream puff without hesitating.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:11.830
- You look so happy. 
- Sweets bring peace into my heart.

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:18.210
Look, mine seems good.
 There's mango in mine.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.650
I'm going to eat this.

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:28.760
- Are you alright, Kaya-san?! 
 - Didn't you collect them all?!

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:34.510
There's no way! The two of them are here! 
 How could it hit Kaya-san and Sunglasses?!

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:37.710
- Was there four of them then?! 
 Who did this?!

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:42.140
- I only made one!  
- So, you made it huh?!

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:47.020
- Oh no!  
- Here taste the project that I made.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.910
It's called "Cutie Papaya".
 How does this taste?!

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:54.220
As my token of appreciation. 
 Taste the scoville!

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.760
It's a dish filled with refreshing colors.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:07.710
A fruit that is round like the sun and green. 
 What could this be?

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:12.720
Very green in color? 
 Could it be a green eggplant?

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.910
- We don't have anything like that here. 
- Oh!

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:20.390
How about a kiwi?!
 It's green when you peel it.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:23.230
The shape is kind of like an eggplant.

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.550
But I think it's not green enough.

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:30.820
- You're right. We should add something green. 
- Oh!

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:33.420
Here are some vibrant greens!

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:34.860
Wasabi

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:40.770
Who made the fourth one then?!

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:17.220
- How are you doing, Yayoi?i 
- I'm doing very well.

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:22.900
- Oh, that's good to hear. 
- I saw an interesting moving picture.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:26.110
What was this moving picture called?

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:30.310
It was--- I forget the title.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.820
Can you tell me what kind of story it was?

00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:35.980
Of course.

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:38.830
It's a story that goes beyond the bounds of time.

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:44.490
It is about a girl that exists over 60 years in time and another boy.

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:49.420
The girl takes the boy through a whirl wind of adventures.

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:53.690
What a great story.

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:57.390
There's a phrase that they always say.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:59.690
What is it?

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:02.950
It was--- uh --- I forget the title.

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:12.290
- My mouth still stings. 
- Are you alright, Hajime-chan?

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:16.850
Thank you Arashi-san!
 You're the only one that's nice to me!

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:23.860
Don't rub your eyes with all that hot stuff!

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:28.030
- Don't rub it! 
- I can't help it! Ouch!

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:32.290
Now you know not to pull any more pranks!

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:38.170
- I can't help it! Men have pride! Can't you understand?
- No I can't!

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:43.100
Arashi-san, I've been thinking.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:47.020
History is not already made.

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:55.440
I'm thinking that the events of the past are set according to the events of the people we bring about.

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:59.000
What do you mean? 
 I don't get it.

00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:02.740
Whether it's the past or the future.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:07.620
We're only moving forward to something unknown.

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:11.130
It's like when I fought "Finger Chopper" Yama.

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:15.000
If I would have gotten scared, I would have been hurt badly.

00:22:15.470 --> 00:22:18.790
But, in order for me to keep from getting hurt, I had to try my best.

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:24.240
It's like today. 
 If we were trying to find the third spicy one...

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:28.130
...would Kaya-san have been able to avoid the "Cutie Q-Chan?"

00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:33.060
Honestly, I don't know.

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:39.670
But, whether our destiny is set or not we shouldn't stop trying.

00:22:41.430 --> 00:22:44.170
I still don't get it.

00:22:44.370 --> 00:22:48.320
I don't get it but I had a lot of fun today!

00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:52.600
- I hope tomorrow is like this too! 
- Yea!

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:56.640
Hey Yasaka! We have a lot of dishes to wash!

00:22:56.890 --> 00:23:00.830
- OK, I'll be right there!  
- It's your turn! Don't try to ditch it!

00:23:01.030 --> 00:23:03.710
I got it! Shut up!

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:11.400
It stings.

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:18.020
It stung a little and it burned a little.

00:23:20.010 --> 00:23:22.130
I wonder if it'll be sunny tomorrow?

00:23:22.270 --> 00:23:24.940
My summer has not ended yet.

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:29.780
The End

00:23:29.780 --> 00:23:34.950
Thank you!
